<p><strong>What learning strategies worked well in this module and
what strategies (or lack of strategy) did not work well? How can you
improve in the next module?</strong><br/>
What learning strategies
worked well:<br/>
Relying directly on the official documentation
(&quot;The Rust Book&quot;) combined with targeted experimentation in
small code snippets helped me grasp strict compiler concepts like
ownership much faster.<br/>
Breaking down the implementation into
small daily milestones (1.5 to 2 hours per day) prevented burnout and
kept steady progress.<br/>
What strategies did not work
well:<br/>
Initially trying to write complex asynchronous or advanced
traits before fully understanding the basic borrowing rules led to
early compilation frustrations.<br/>
How I can improve in the next
module:<br/>
For the next module, I plan to spend more time during
the planning phase writing small prototype functions to test
unfamiliar syntax before diving into the main implementation, which
will reduce troubleshooting time.</p>
